{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1510-denominator-gradient-injury-rates.md", "equation": "Poisson model log E[y] = log(m) + a + b·x vs per-appearance logistic; the identifying comparison is fixed-90 vs recorded-minutes offset, holding family/link/rows fixed (only the offset changes). γ fitted as OLS of log recorded minutes on previous-seven-day club minutes per 90, with weekly/half-weekly calendar-phase terms, covariance clustered on player (refit under club-season and fixture clustering as checks). Two defects separated empirically: (a) outcome truncation isolated by replacing event rows' minutes with the non-event lineup-role mean and refitting; (b) exposure dependence isolated by refitting denominators within every lineup stratum and by adjusting vs restricting on squad role. Attenuation measured by fitting one Poisson model twice, changing nothing but the offset, with 1,000 player-resamples for intervals. Attenuation-vs-γ relationship traced by sweeping a floor on recorde ...", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9134}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1510-denominator-gradient-injury-rates.md", "equation": "Denominator identity (to first order): log E[y] = log(m) + a + b_off·x and log E[y] = a′ + b_app·x imply b_off = b_app − γ, where γ = ∂log(m)/∂x. Poisson with log workload entered as offset ≡ log workload as covariate with coefficient fixed at 1 (Shrier et al.); where a risk factor changes workload, including workload biases the estimate — overadjustment / control for a variable on the exposure→outcome path. Negligible threshold γ < 0.05 (a reporting convention: at γ=0.05 the measured attenuation ratio is 1.20, i.e. ~4.1% of the rate ratio). Assumptions: (1) Poisson/log-linear mean structure for injury counts; (2) same-day spell start = public injury report (explicitly NOT a clinical diagnosis or verified time loss; outcome sensitivity unknown — second blinded audit queue returned no verdict); (3) minutes reconstructed from reports are accurate; (4) identity approximations hold while γ i ...", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9134}
